From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] edma_v2: include edma_dp_vp.h so edma_dp_vp_xmit() has a prototype

edma_v2/edma_dp_vp.c:26:13: error: no previous prototype for 'edma_dp_vp_xmit'
  [-Werror=missing-prototypes]

Same class as the qca-ssdk "include your own header" fixes: the
function's declaration lives in edma_dp_vp.h, but the .c file never
includes it (edma_dp.c gets the prototype indirectly when it takes the
address for .vp_xmit).  Linux 6.10 turned on -Wmissing-prototypes.

Class: mainline-replaces-API (compiler policy tightened on a genuine
missing-include bug).
diff -ruN a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_dp_vp.c b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_dp_vp.c
--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_dp_vp.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v2/edma_dp_vp.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include "edma_regs.h"
 #include "edma_debug.h"
 #include "edma.h"
+#include "edma_dp_vp.h"
 
 /*
  * edma_dp_vp_xmit()
